  <prompt>
    Implement FR-23: a richer comment-thread UI. Comments render as threads showing author, timestamp, and
    replies; the user can view, create, reply to, and resolve a thread. Threads persist as native `w:comment`
    on save (via the existing R2 comment-anchor mark + writer path) and the thread model is the render target
    that FR-25 (import existing Word comment threads, task 051) will feed into on round-trip. SCOPE GUARD
    (binding): view/create/reply/resolve ONLY — NOT full Word comment-feature parity (spec FR-23 + Assumptions:
    "nested reply chains beyond one level render flat if the source lacks the modern-comments 4-part
    structure"). Client-only, on the MIT TipTap base + Fluent v9; NO TipTap product feature (paid or unpaid),
    no `@tiptap-pro/*` Comments module.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Senior React/TypeScript engineer fluent in TipTap 3 / ProseMirror inline marks, Fluent UI v9, and thread/
    reply UI modeling. Understands how the existing `CommentAnchorMark` anchors a comment to a range and how a
    thread (author/timestamp/replies/resolved) is the UI layer over those anchors, persisted as `w:comment`.
  </role>

  <goal>
    A comment-thread UI (component + hook + thread type) over the existing `CommentAnchorMark`: threads show
    author + timestamp + replies; the user can create a thread on a selection, reply to a thread, and resolve
    it; threads persist as native `w:comment` on save. The thread data model is shaped so FR-25 (task 051) can
    project imported `RecoveredComment` threads into the same render surface. Matching component tests assert
    thread rendering (author/timestamp), reply, resolve, persistence-shape, and the scope-guard flat-render of
    deeper reply chains, plus an ADR-021 dark-mode render check.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      R2 shipped the home-grown comment marks → `w:comment` path (design §7.5 "Comments | Home-grown marks →
      w:comment (shipped, R2)"); the anchor mark is `CommentAnchorMark.ts`. R3 makes the comment SURFACE
      richer — real threads with author/timestamp/replies and resolve — as a table-stakes credibility tool
      and, critically, as the render target for FR-25 import (task 051 projects `RecoveredComment` threads
      into this UI on Load, and FR-26 keeps them across save). This is a client-only task; the persistence path
      to `w:comment` already exists (R2 `DocxAnnotationWriter`). SCOPE GUARD keeps it short of full Word
      comment parity.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="new">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/widgets/ComposeCommentThread.tsx — NEW Fluent v9 thread UI: author, timestamp, replies, create/reply/resolve affordances</file>
      <file role="new">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/widgets/hooks/useComposeCommentThreads.ts — NEW hook: thread/reply state over `CommentAnchorMark`; create/reply/resolve; expose a thread model for persistence + FR-25 import</file>
      <file role="new">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/widgets/ComposeCommentThread.types.ts — NEW thread data model (author, timestamp, replies, resolved) shaped for FR-25 `RecoveredComment` projection</file>
      <file role="modify">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/widgets/ComposeEditor.tsx — mount the comment-thread surface; wire selection → create-thread</file>
      <file role="canonical-reuse">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/widgets/marks/CommentAnchorMark.ts — the existing comment-anchor mark threads render over; reuse, do NOT reimplement anchoring</file>
      <file role="reference">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/widgets/ComposeReanchorBanner.tsx — Fluent v9 conventions to mirror</file>
      <file role="export">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/index.ts — export the thread UI + type (FR-25/task 051 consumes the type)</file>
      <file role="design">projects/spaarkeai-compose-r3/design.md §7.5 (Comments = shipped R2 marks → w:comment); spec.md FR-23 + FR-25/FR-26 + Assumptions (thread depth scope guard)</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="none" status="n/a">Independent — no task dependency. Runs in the W4 toolset parallel wave alongside 040/042/043. NOTE: task 051 (FR-25 import comments) deps on THIS task (044) — the thread model authored here is 051's render target.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project / owner rule 2026-07-14">NO TipTap product feature (paid or unpaid) — no `@tiptap-pro/*` Comments module. Home-grown thread UI over the existing `CommentAnchorMark` + Fluent v9 only.</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-03 / project">If any npm extension is touched, verify it resolves to `@tiptap/extension-*` (MIT), NEVER `@tiptap-pro/*`. No new dependency expected.</constraint>
    <constraint source="FR-23 SCOPE GUARD / spec Assumptions">view/create/reply/resolve ONLY — NOT full Word comment-feature parity. Nested reply chains beyond one level render FLAT if the source lacks the modern-comments 4-part structure.</constraint>
    <constraint source="FR-23 / FR-25">Threads MUST persist as native `w:comment` on save (via the existing R2 writer path). The thread data model MUST be shaped so FR-25 (task 051) can project imported `RecoveredComment` threads into the same render surface — do not fork a parallel thread shape.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-021 / NFR-10">The thread UI is Fluent UI v9 and MUST render correctly in dark mode (theme tokens; no hard-coded colors).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028 / NFR-10">No new network calls; any client fetch uses `@spaarke/auth`.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038 / NFR-06">Client component/unit tests only; no `Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;`, no DI-registration/ctor-null tests. Tests exercise real thread state (render/reply/resolve) and the flat-render scope guard.</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §11">New thread UI component — provide the `&lt;justification&gt;` (Existing / Extension / Cost-of-doing-nothing).</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>ProseMirror comment-anchor marks; thread/reply UI modeling; native w:comment persistence; Fluent v9 + dark mode</topic>
    <files>
      <file>src/client/pcf/CLAUDE.md</file>
