    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="Comment anchor mark" location="src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/widgets/marks/CommentAnchorMark.ts">
        The existing comment-anchor mark ties a comment to a range; threads render over these anchors. Reuse — do not reimplement anchoring or the `w:comment` persistence path.
      </pattern>
      <pattern name="Fluent v9 surface conventions" location="src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/widgets/ComposeReanchorBanner.tsx">
        Mirror the Fluent v9 token usage + dark-mode-safe styling for the thread cards + reply affordances.
      </pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Declare FULL rigor. Load the knowledge files + design §7.5 + the FR-23 scope guard + FR-25/FR-26 (so the thread model fits import). Read `CommentAnchorMark.ts`.</step>
    <step order="1" name="Thread data model">Define `ComposeCommentThread.types.ts`: a thread with author, timestamp, ordered replies, and resolved state — shaped so FR-25's `RecoveredComment` (task 051) projects into it without a parallel shape.</step>
    <step order="2" name="Thread state hook">Implement `useComposeCommentThreads.ts` over `CommentAnchorMark`: create a thread on a selection, reply, resolve; expose the thread model for persistence (native `w:comment`) and for FR-25 import.</step>
    <step order="3" name="Thread UI">Build `ComposeCommentThread.tsx`: render author + timestamp + replies; create/reply/resolve affordances. Deeper-than-one-level reply chains render FLAT per the scope guard. Fluent v9; verify dark mode.</step>
    <step order="4" name="Wire into editor">Mount the thread surface in `ComposeEditor.tsx`; wire selection → create-thread; export the component + type from `index.ts` (task 051 consumes the type).</step>
    <step order="5" name="Tests">Author component tests: thread renders author+timestamp; reply appends; resolve marks resolved; the model persists in the `w:comment`-compatible shape; deeper reply chains render flat (scope guard); include an ADR-021 dark-mode render check.</step>
    <step order="6" name="Verify">`npm run build` the shared lib; run the new tests. Update TASK-INDEX status.</step>
  </steps>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/widgets/ComposeCommentThread.tsx</output>
    <output type="code">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/widgets/hooks/useComposeCommentThreads.ts</output>
    <output type="code">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/widgets/ComposeCommentThread.types.ts</output>
    <output type="code">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/widgets/ComposeEditor.tsx (thread surface mounted)</output>
    <output type="test">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/widgets/ComposeCommentThread.test.tsx</output>
  </outputs>

  <justification>
    <existing>R2 shipped `CommentAnchorMark.ts` (the anchor mark) and the `w:comment` writer path, but there is NO thread UI — no author/timestamp/reply/resolve surface. `ComposeReanchorBanner.tsx` is a re-anchor banner, unrelated. No overlap.</existing>
    <extension>Cannot fold into `CommentAnchorMark` (a ProseMirror mark, not a React UI) nor into any existing banner. A thread UI with reply/resolve state is a cohesive new surface warranting its own component + hook + type; it reuses the existing anchor mark + `w:comment` persistence rather than adding new marks or a new writer.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Without it, comments cannot be viewed as threads with author/timestamp or replied to/resolved — and FR-25 (import existing Word comment threads, task 051) has no render target, so imported threads cannot be shown. Concrete failing contracts: FR-23 acceptance "a comment thread shows author+timestamp and supports a reply; persists as w:comment" and FR-25's dependency on this render surface both fail.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <acceptance-criteria testable="true">
    <criterion testable="true">A comment thread renders with author and timestamp — a unit test asserts both appear for a thread.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A user can create a thread on a selection, reply to a thread (reply appends in order), and resolve a thread (resolved state set) — unit tests assert each.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Threads persist in a shape that maps to native `w:comment` on save (the existing R2 writer path); a test asserts the persistence-shape of the thread model.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The thread data model is shaped so FR-25's imported `RecoveredComment` threads (task 051) project into the same render surface — no parallel thread shape is introduced.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">SCOPE GUARD: reply chains deeper than one level render flat when the source lacks the modern-comments 4-part structure — a test asserts flat rendering; no full-Word-parity comment features are added.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">No `@tiptap-pro/*` dependency and no TipTap product Comments feature is added.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The thread UI renders correctly in Fluent v9 dark mode (ADR-021).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Matching component tests exist and pass; shared-lib `npm run build` is green.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <ui-tests>
    <ui-test name="Thread shows author and timestamp">
      <steps>Create a comment on a selection with a known author; open the thread.</steps>
      <expected>The thread card shows the author name and a timestamp.</expected>
    </ui-test>
    <ui-test name="Reply appends to thread">
      <steps>Open an existing thread, type a reply, submit.</steps>
      <expected>The reply appears appended below the original comment in order.</expected>
    </ui-test>
    <ui-test name="Resolve a thread">
      <steps>Click Resolve on an open thread.</steps>
      <expected>The thread is marked resolved (visually distinct / collapsed) and its resolved state is set.</expected>
    </ui-test>
    <ui-test name="Deep reply chain renders flat (scope guard)">
      <steps>Load a thread whose source lacks the modern-comments 4-part structure but has multiple replies.</steps>
      <expected>Replies render as a flat list (one level), not a nested tree.</expected>
    </ui-test>
    <ui-test name="Dark-mode render (ADR-021)">
      <steps>Render the comment-thread UI under the Fluent v9 dark theme provider.</steps>
      <expected>Thread cards, replies, and affordances use theme tokens and are legible in dark mode; no hard-coded light colors.</expected>
    </ui-test>
  </ui-tests>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
  </execution>
</task>
